# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages. Do not wrap it in `<main>`, flex shells, or page layouts.

- DO NOT add dynamic safe-area bottom padding or margins (`pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]`, `pb-safe`, `mb-safe`, or extra `pb-*` utilities) to the bottom `<nav>` container or its child elements.
- The bottom navigation bar container MUST remain `fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 h-[50px] w-full bg-background border-t border-border/30`.
- Inner content wrapper MUST utilize `flex h-full w-full items-center justify-around px-2` to keep icons anchored flush at the lowest margin without floating upward.
- Do NOT modify or recalculate this bottom navigation bar component when editing page-level layouts or components.

Page scroll clearance stays on `main.app-scroll` as `pb-[60px]`. That is not nav padding; do not move it onto the `<nav>`.
